From ac779ec34bc8adcd45ae1d012b3dd4ab7e5d2391 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rong Zhang <i@rong.moe>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 466/468] AOSCOS: MIPS: page: Use GPR number macros on
 CPU_LOONGSON64

Since commit 6aec8e0502fe ("MIPS: page: Use GPR number macros"),
unprefixed ABI names of GPRs are gone, causing build failure with
CONFIG_CPU_LOONGSON64.

In previous releases, the Fixes: commit was guard by #ifdef
CONFIG_CPU_LOONGSON3, which has long gone since commit 268a2d60013049
("MIPS: Loongson64: Rename CPU TYPES"), so the error was never
triggered.

Fix it by using GPR number macros.

Fixes: "AOSCOS: Optimize clear_page"
Signed-off-by: Rong Zhang <i@rong.moe>
---
 arch/mips/mm/page.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/mm/page.c b/arch/mips/mm/page.c
index 23a000453aeda..6c7967b1a38c1 100644
--- a/arch/mips/mm/page.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mm/page.c
@@ -226,7 +226,7 @@ static void set_prefetch_parameters(void)
 static void build_clear_store(u32 **buf, int off)
 {
 #ifdef CONFIG_CPU_LOONGSON64
-	uasm_i_gssq(buf, ZERO, ZERO, off, A0);
+	uasm_i_gssq(buf, GPR_ZERO, GPR_ZERO, off, GPR_A0);
 #else
 	if (cpu_has_64bit_gp_regs || cpu_has_64bit_zero_reg) {
 		uasm_i_sd(buf, GPR_ZERO, off, GPR_A0);
-- 
2.56.0

